Revision history for oEdtk

2.1129      2026-10-19
    - Tracking: ED_SOURCE now names the input file actually processed by the packaged tracker (its --csvInsert, --csvDistrib or --csvIdCheck file). A run that handles no file (--insert, --stats, --sql, table maintenance) leaves the field empty instead of writing the old "input-file" placeholder. oEdtk::Tracking->new keeps an explicit empty source and falls back to @ARGV only when the source is omitted.
    - Tracking: a row written without a message now carries the name of the function that recorded it in ED_MESSAGE, instead of a blank or a lone space. The Tracking package and its signal-handler closures are skipped so the caller's code is named; both oEdtk::Tracking and the legacy duplicate oEdtk::Tracking2 follow the rule.
    - tracker: an --insert row without ED_MESSAGE names main::insert_trackline, and the show_table helper passes ED_SOURCE as the positional source (the old named source parameter was ignored by the constructor).
    - tests: new t/41_tracking_fields.t pins the source and message rules against an in-memory SQLite database, including the empty-source constructor path.
    - All modules of the oEdtk package are realigned on the package version 2.1129; the frozen duplicate lib/oEdtk/logger2.pm follows, so its sha256 pin in t/int/67_logger_normalization.t is re-baselined.

2.1128      2026-10-19
    - Style: every Perl file under lib/, t/, tools/ and tracker/ is now perltidy-clean with the repository .perltidyrc. The 15 files that were not (8 under tools/, 7 under tracker/) were reformatted; tools/deparse_equiv.sh proves the pass semantics-preserving for all 212 files.
    - perlcritic: severity-5 violations drop from 41 to 1 across the tree. Legacy scripts lose subroutine prototypes, explicit 'return undef', two-argument open calls, a bareword filehandle and an unnecessary 'no strict refs'; strictures are enabled where they were missing. The remaining violation is the deliberate leading-zero octal '01' in lib/oEdtk/lib/cob2pm.pl, left untouched on request.
    - tests: T05, T09, d33 and T67 stay green, as does the full suite apart from the four known pre-existing failures (T03, T15, T50, T58).
    - All modules of the oEdtk package are realigned on the package version 2.1128; the frozen duplicate lib/oEdtk/logger2.pm follows, so its sha256 pin in t/int/67_logger_normalization.t is re-baselined.

2.1127      2026-10-19
    - Dependencies: Text::QRCode becomes an optional runtime dependency. It builds against the native libqrencode library, so making it mandatory made a plain 'cpan oEdtk' fail on hosts without it (notably Windows) before anything was installed. oEdtk::TexDoc no longer loads it at compile time; append_qr_code requires it on first use and croaks with an explicit message when it is absent. The module now sits under META_MERGE runtime recommends, so a recommended module is still never eagerly used (T06).
    - Dependencies: DBD::mysql and DBD::Pg leave TEST_REQUIRES; they were already runtime recommends. 'cpan oEdtk' no longer tries to build the MySQL driver (which needs mysql_config) or the PostgreSQL driver just to install the package. DBD::Oracle was already out, and DBD::MariaDB was never declared (MariaDB is reached through DBD::mysql).
    - tests: the PostgreSQL integration facets (d02, d20 to d28) and the MySQL facet (d30) skip with an explicit reason when the driver is missing; t/int/37_texdoc.t skips the QR emission facet when Text::QRCode is absent while still checking the argument errors. When the driver and its OEDTK_TEST_*_ON flag are present, the tests run unchanged.
    - cpanfile regenerated from Makefile.PL: Text::QRCode moves to recommends and the test block no longer declares DBD::Pg / DBD::mysql.
    - README: Text::QRCode moves to a new 'Optional modules' section, and the database-driver and test-extra sections state that the engine drivers are optional and the facets skip without them.
    - All modules of the oEdtk package are realigned on the package version 2.1127; the frozen duplicate lib/oEdtk/logger2.pm follows, so its sha256 pin in t/int/67_logger_normalization.t is re-baselined.

2.1126      2026-10-18
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: new caller parameter force_copy (true) forces the parsed PostgreSQL COPY path ahead of pg_copy_staging, burst_mo and EDTK_DB_BURST_MO, so an operator can bypass the ELT staging path before a large import starts. The decision reason is logged as 'force_copy => 1'. The packaged tracker exposes it as --forceCopy for --csvInsert, --csvDistrib and --csvIdCheck.
    - POD: EDTK_DB_BURST_MO now documents the shipped 50 MiB default; the old '0 is the shipped value' claim was stale.
    - tests: t/30_dbadmin_pure.t pins the force_copy precedence without a database, and t/int/d21_burst_threshold.t gains a PostgreSQL facet proving the COPY path is taken even when pg_copy_staging and burst_mo would select ELT.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: the edtk_admin action duration is now truncated to whole seconds through the new _elapsed_seconds helper. DBAdmin imports time() from Time::HiRes, so the raw time - $time delta was fractional and PostgreSQL rejected it on the integer column edtk_admin.ed_action_duration, leaving the action open in START. The three update sites (acheck_request_for_db, acheck_db_admin_on_connect and _db_with_lock) go through the helper; t/30_dbadmin_pure.t pins it without a database.
    - All modules of the oEdtk package are realigned on the package version 2.1126; the frozen duplicate lib/oEdtk/logger2.pm follows, so its sha256 pin in t/int/67_logger_normalization.t is re-baselined.

2.1125      2026-10-17
    - The stale-schema remediation hint is now portable and copy-pasteable. oEdtk::DBAdmin::_schema_fix_command single-quotes the DSN and the user (an unquoted 'dbi:...;host=...' was split by the shell on its semicolons) and honours a host-registered renderer, the package variable $SCHEMA_FIX_HINT: when set to a code ref, it renders the hint instead, so a packaged host can name a command it can actually run. The default form is otherwise unchanged and the password stays a bare '<pass>' placeholder. A host hook that dies or returns nothing falls back to the default form.
    - New READ-ONLY schema_AdditivePlan($dbh, %opt): the in-place additive update as a plan -- the missing columns, the wider ones, the missing tables, the key and the unsupported widens -- computed without writing anything. Exported alongside schema_Additive. db_migrate.pl gains the matching '--additive --dry-run' preview.
    - The packaged tracker (tracker/dev/tracker.pl) gains an in-place '--upgradeSchema --additive' sub-mode with a '--additive --dryRun' read-only preview, and registers $oEdtk::DBAdmin::SCHEMA_FIX_HINT so the stale-schema hint it may log names 'edtk-track --upgradeSchema --additive' rather than the source-only lib/db_migrate.pl.
    - tests: new t/int/68_schema_additive_plan.t (T68) pins the plan shapes and proves the base is untouched; t/int/66_schema_stale_warn.t (T66) gains facets for the quoted default hint and for the host override.
    - All modules of the oEdtk package are realigned on the package version 2.1125: oEdtk.pm goes 2.1124 -> 2.1125 and the other 51 modules, which carried 2.1124, follow it, each keeping its own style (quoted or bare). The frozen duplicate lib/oEdtk/logger2.pm follows too, so its sha256 pin in t/int/67_logger_normalization.t is re-baselined.

2.1124      2026-10-16
    - Performance pass over oEdtk and oEUser, driven by Devel::NYTProf: four measured hotspots are optimised, each proven semantics-preserving by an in-process A/B and the golden witnesses -- the oEdtk::RecordParser seek plan, the oEdtk::Config ini memoisation, the oEdtk::Main signed-amount table hoisted out of the per-call build, and the oEUser::Descriptor::load id -> descriptor dispatch. Two further plan targets were measured and deliberately left as they were, and one (oEdtk::TexTag::escape_0) was found to be unreachable dead code. Per-item before/after and the reproduction commands are in docs/perf/P80-rapport.md.
    - All modules of the oEdtk package now carry the package version 2.1124: oEdtk.pm goes 2.1120 -> 2.1124 and the other modules, which carried a mix of 0.01, 0.14, 1.0, 1.5NNN, 1.9NNN and 2.11NN, are aligned on it.
    - Documentation updated: the performance campaign (docs/perf/) and the integration, DBAdmin and logger contracts (docs/integration/) are brought in step with the released tree.
    - Licence: the text shipped as lib/oEdtk/COPYING is the Artistic License 2.0 named by the oEdtk POD.

2.1110      2026-10-13
    - Integration of the 0.8032 fork, phase S10 (declarative metadata only; no behaviour change).
    - oEdtk.pm: $VERSION 2.1109 -> 2.1110.
    - Makefile.PL: MIN_PERL_VERSION raised to 5.028 (D3) and the ExtUtils::MakeMaker floor to 6.64, which TEST_REQUIRES needs. PREREQ_PM gains the fork's runtime dependencies (Data::UUID, File::Slurp, HTTP::Request, HTTP::Status, IO::Socket::SSL, IPC::Run3, JSON::PP, LWP::UserAgent, PDF::Tk, Readonly, Regexp::Common, Term::ANSIColor, Text::CSV_XS, Text::QRCode, Time::HiRes, Try::Tiny, YAML::Tiny); the ones that are core at 5.028 are listed for explicitness. TEST_REQUIRES declares the test and database tooling. META_MERGE targets meta-spec 2; there is no recommends (the S10 gate kept every fork dependency as a hard requirement). The oEUser distribution stays out of the prerequisites (at most a suggests).
    - cpanfile is now generated from Makefile.PL by tools/gen_cpanfile.pl, the single source of truth; it no longer carries the fork's dead cpanfile dependencies (XML::Parser, XML::Encoding, Mail::Sender, Barcode::DataMatrix, PDF::API2, Hash::Merge::Simple, Hash::Flatten, MIME::Lite, Email::Valid, Locale::PO, XML::LibXSLT, Text::Unaccent::PurePerl).
    - tests: new t/int/06_dist.t (T06) pins the Perl floor, the cpanfile/Makefile.PL identity and the requires/recommends split against the ratchet t/data/dist_prereq_gap.txt.
    - Integration of the 0.8032 fork, phase S11: the shipped template lib/oEdtk/iniEdtk/tplate.edtk.ini is rebuilt as the union of the mainline (M) keys and the shared witness ini keys, with defaults that keep the M behaviour. It gains the fork service keys, inactive by default (NWS_EMAILING_URI, KEYCLOAK_URL / KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID / KEYCLOAK_SECRET_ID, DISSEMINATION_PLAN_URL), in a new [SERVICES] section, plus the ed_idjob primary-key keys EDTK_DB_PK_IDJOB (yes, mainline) and EDTK_DB_IDJOB_DEFAULT (empty until the S51 gate), the DBAdmin case-folding key EDTK_DB_FetchHashKeyName and the log-level key EDTK_LOG_LVL. EDTK_EXT_COMSET stays (removed at S33). The two U+FFFD and two U+200B marks carried by the old file are repaired and the accented subject text is restored; the file stays UTF-8 with CRLF. The one shared edtk.ini is untouched.
    - tests: new t/int/07_anonymised.t (T07) hunts residual production identifiers against the out-of-repo blacklist EDTK_ANON_BLACKLIST over the shipped tree and the shared ini, and ratchets the class of the shared ini secret keys (t/data/shared_ini_secrets.txt); t/int/15_config.t (T15) now also checks that the template documents every key of the shared ini and carries the fork keys.
    - Integration of the 0.8032 fork, phase S12 (static files): the three shipped forms lib/oEdtk/lib/html/edtk_ged.html, edtk_inged.html and index.html now carry the fork content, fully anonymised (D7). The client values are replaced by the neutral placeholders the mainline already used (APP_n, CORP_n, group_1, AUTRE); index.html gains the three fork-only applications as APP_5..APP_7. lib/oEdtk/lib/template/runEdtk.pl loses the trailing spaces of its first two lines. lang/ is unchanged.
    - tests: t/int/07_anonymised.t (T07) gains a facet that ratchets the option vocabulary of the three static forms against t/data/html_options.txt, so a real client value cannot be re-introduced.
    - Integration of the 0.8032 fork, phase S13 (mechanical tidy, no behaviour change): the existing Perl tree is reformatted with the frozen .perltidyrc (100-column lines, TAB indentation, -enc=none, input line endings kept). The pass is proven semantics-preserving file by file (perl -MO=Deparse before/after, with a PPI token-stream fallback for the few files B::Deparse cannot render, e.g. lib/oEdtk/Main.pm); the changes are pure reformatting (line breaks, brace and parenthesis spacing, and a handful of provably neutral token clean-ups such as a dropped empty list element or heredoc-opener spacing). 88 files under lib/oEdtk/ and t/ are reformatted. Excluded: the three legacy editor modules (removed at S33) and lib/oEdtk/lib/edms_runner.pl, which carries a pre-existing syntax error perltidy cannot parse with confidence.
    - tools/tidy_all.sh drives the pass (it reformats to a temporary file and only replaces the original on success); tools/deparse_equiv.sh snapshots and compares the pre/post equivalence keys; tools/tidy_exclusions.txt records the excluded paths.
    - tests: t/int/09_style.t (T09) now guards the whole tree, not just the files rewritten at S02: its tidy set is every .pm/.pl/.cgi/.t under lib/ and t/ minus the recorded exclusions, and its perltidy invocation matches tools/tidy_all.sh exactly (-enc=none -ple). The perlcritic baseline (severity 5) is re-measured and unchanged. The suite is 525 tests over 34 files.
    - Integration of the 0.8032 fork, phase S14: the fork companion distribution oEUser is created at oEUser/ (version 0.10), gathering unchanged the fork's user-side modules (oEUser::Lib, oEUser::ECM, oEUser::Descriptor and its generated descriptors, and the oEUser::XML::Cameleon / Coheris / Default / Generic readers), with a rebuilt MANIFEST and a Makefile.PL that declares the real prerequisites (oEdtk >= 2.1110). Its hand-written modules are reformatted with the repository .perltidyrc; the generated descriptors are left as generated and only compile-checked. Its suite is new: t/60_load.t loads every module (oEUser::Lib is recorded as a gap until oEdtk::Utils lands in oEdtk at S23) and t/66_dist.t keeps MANIFEST in step; tools/run-tnr.sh runs it. In the mainline tree, t/data/encoding_legacy.txt gains the three generated descriptors that carry CRLF from the fork.
    - Integration of the 0.8032 fork, phase S20 (pure logic): oEdtk.pm's $VERSION goes 2.1110 -> 2.1111, the first delivered code of phase P2. Three fork modules land at their final generic home under lib/oEdtk/ and gain POD: oEdtk::IBAN (IBAN / BIC validation), whose latent bug is fixed -- iban_letter_to_number read the global $1 instead of its argument, so it only worked from inside is_valid_iban_checksum's s///e and returned -55 when called directly; oEdtk::Restitution (follow_path / restitution_value), which gains the missing "use feature 'say'"; and oEdtk::FixIdx (make every document of a CSV index span an even number of pages). The corporate document-type typology moves to the oEUser distribution as oEUser::Constants, keeping its French reference data verbatim; the generic oEdtk::Constants stays under the old name as a thin delegate that loads oEUser::Constants on demand and fails cleanly when oEUser is absent. The T02 gap ratchet loses the four now-resolved whole-module lines. The ported fixidx sample pair carries the generic tree's corporate-name anonymisation (the brand is replaced by CORP). The oEUser MANIFEST registers the two new files, and the witness-M golden is recaptured for the new banner.
    - tests: new t/int/30_iban.t (T30: the fork's nine IBAN/BIC checks plus a dedicated test of the fixed iban_letter_to_number), t/int/32_fixidx.t (T32: the fork's index sample pair), t/int/36_restitution.t (T36: follow_path) and oEUser/t/20_moved_modules.t (T62: oEUser::Constants and the oEdtk::Constants delegate). The suite is 546 tests over 37 files (root) and 15 tests over 3 files (oEUser).
    - Integration of the 0.8032 fork, phase S21 (XML): the fork's DTD/XSD validators land under lib/oEdtk/XML/ and the generic XML readers move out of oEUser. oEdtk::XML::DTD merges the fork's oEdtk::XML::DTD and oEdtk::XML::DTD::Utils (about 90% identical) and fixes the undefined publicId -- a document without a DOCTYPE exposed the DTD node as undef and died on its ->publicId, and reading it through externalSubset both returned undef and corrupted the node's ownership, double-freeing on a later is_valid. oEdtk::XML::DTD::Utils stays loadable as a delegate for the fork's parked callers; oEdtk::XML::XSD holds the XSD validator. oEUser::XML::Default and oEUser::XML::Generic move to oEdtk::XML::Default and oEdtk::XML::Generic (D23); the old oEUser names remain as thin delegates and Cameleon / Coheris stay in oEUser. Two fork bugs in the readers are fixed: xml_verif croaked on a valid document (its XML::LibXML::Schema::validate check was inverted) and its schema lookup interpolated "$name.$ext", doubling the dot ("data..xsd") so it never found the schema next to the document. The ported modules need no new prerequisite -- the fork's Hash::Merge::Simple, Exporter::Shiny and XML::LibXML::Reader are not pulled in (the readers use core Exporter and a plain hash merge, the DTD uses XML::LibXML's own node-type constants) -- so the T06 prerequisite ratchet is unchanged.
    - tests: new t/int/35_xml_dtd_xsd.t (T35: DTD found_in_list / validate_xml / xml_to_txt, the XSD validator and the DTD::Utils delegate), t/int/42_xml_readers.t (T42: xml_open, the fixed xml_verif polarity and the XML::Default reader) and oEUser/t/10_delegates.t (T61, XML facet). The T02 gap ratchet loses the three XML whole-module lines. The suite is 560 tests over 39 files (root) and 18 tests over 4 files (oEUser).
    - Integration of the 0.8032 fork, phase S22a (network clients): the fork's three service clients land in the oEUser companion distribution (gate answer: all three in oEUser, Keycloak included). oEUser::Keycloak (get_token / token_url) fetches a bearer token; its realm becomes the configuration key KEYCLOAK_REALM (default serverToServer) and a missing key is fatal and named. oEUser::Emailing (send_mail) posts to NWS_EMAILING_URI + /emails; the template name and User-Agent string the fork hard-coded become EMAILING_TEMPLATE / EMAILING_USER_AGENT with the fork values as defaults, and the payload is built by a separate build_request. The fork bug in it is fixed: it called JSON::encode_json while importing only JSON::PP, so every send died at the encode line. oEUser::DisseminationPlan (idx1_app_idlot / idx1_line / call_plan) reads the idx1 CSV of a lot and posts one entry per distinct document; the missing "use Cwd" it silently relied on is added, File::Slurp::read_file becomes a core slurp, and the unused "use oEdtk::Main" (whose load prints the oEdtk banner) and the corporate __DATA__ block are dropped. Transport security is factored into a new shared oEUser::Net (ua_ssl_opts / make_ua): peer and host-name verification are ON by default, EDTK_SSL_VERIFY (0/no/false/off) turns them off and EDTK_SSL_CA_PATH pins a CA file or directory, replacing the fork's hard-coded verify_hostname => 0 and its private corporate CA. In the mainline tree the old names stay available as thin generic delegates lib/oEdtk/Keycloak.pm, lib/oEdtk/Emailing.pm and lib/oEdtk/DisseminationPlan.pm that load the oEUser module on demand and fail cleanly when oEUser is absent. The T02 gap ratchet loses the three now-resolved whole-module lines; the oEUser MANIFEST registers the four new files; the shipped template gains KEYCLOAK_REALM, EMAILING_TEMPLATE, EMAILING_USER_AGENT, EDTK_SSL_VERIFY and EDTK_SSL_CA_PATH in [SERVICES] (CRLF kept).
    - tests: new t/int/34_network_mocks.t (T34: the oEUser::Net safe defaults, a token fetch through the generic oEdtk::Keycloak delegate against a mock server, a non-200 token being fatal with its body, a missing key being named, and the three delegates exposing the fork symbols); oEUser/t/20_moved_modules.t (T62) gains the e-mailing and dissemination-plan facets (payload shape, a send round trip, and the per-document de-duplication 1,1,2 -> two posts). The mock helper t/lib/oEdtkTest.pm::fake_httpd is fixed (it never called Test::Fake::HTTPD->run, so endpoint/port reported 0). The suite is 568 tests over 40 files (root) and 21 tests over 4 files (oEUser).
    - Integration of the 0.8032 fork, phase S22b (ECM): the ECM injector the fork kept in oEUser::ECM lands in the generic distribution as oEdtk::ECM (D22), its generic home because it is the default EDTK_ACQUIT_API implementation and so must work without oEUser. The REST contract is unchanged: send_document uploads a file with its index metadata as a JSON "text" form part to POST /v1/documents/upload?apirole=EDITIQUE (expects 201), and http_put_envoidate_for_iddoc stamps MAILED plus an envoi_date on an existing document via PUT /v1/documents/<id>?apirole=EDITIQUE (expects 200); the fork's fixed "T12:MM:SS" date form is kept on the wire. The audit corrects the plan on one point: ECM does not fetch a Keycloak token, it presents a static API key verbatim in the Authorization header, so oEdtk::Keycloak is not involved. The base URL and that key become the configuration keys APIECM_URL and APIECM_APIKEY_EDITIQUE; each function gains an optional trailing configuration hashref (the fork's two-argument form still defaults to config_read) and the private _get_file_content is kept. The hard-coded corporate CA and the disabled host-name verification are replaced by the shared safe-by-default transport, which moves up from oEUser::Net to the generic oEdtk::Net (ua_ssl_opts / make_ua); the oEUser::Net name stays a thin delegate, so the S22a clients are untouched. The two French error messages become English and the corporate reference is dropped. The fork's oEUser::ECM name stays a delegate forwarding the three functions. The shipped template gains APIECM_URL and APIECM_APIKEY_EDITIQUE in [SERVICES] (CRLF kept), and Makefile.PL declares the HTTP::Request::Common prerequisite the ported module uses (cpanfile regenerated).
    - tests: new t/int/41_ecm.t (T41: the upload and mailed-date wire contracts against a fake server, a fatal non-201 / non-200 with their bodies, a missing configuration key being named before any request is sent, the two keys documented in the template, and the delegate emitting the same requests as oEdtk::ECM); oEUser/t/10_delegates.t (T61) gains the ECM facet; t/int/15_config.t (T15) counts the two new keys among the fork service keys. The suite is 598 tests over 41 files (root) and 22 tests over 4 files (oEUser).
    - Integration of the 0.8032 fork, phase S23 (extensions and the last generic modules): the fork's oEdtk::Utils is split along its corporate seam. The generic half lands in lib/oEdtk/Utils.pm (text cleanup, the LaTeX index format IDX_FORMAT, the date/price parsers, the tracking helpers track_begin/track/track_end, and small value helpers); the corporate half -- init and the INDEX_* accessors, which call oEUser::Lib or name corporate schema identifiers -- moves to oEUser::Utils, and the generic module keeps the same names as delegates that load oEUser on demand and fail cleanly without it. The fork exported delete_useless_whitespaces while leaving it out of @EXPORT_OK (its own test imported it), so it is exported here, together with kill_non_latin_1_9_chars_in_place. The fork's oEdtk::LaTeX lands as lib/oEdtk/LaTeX.pm (latin-9 escaping, the small TeX builders, make_index) and defines the three names it exported but never defined (demo_write, demo_expected_write, unfold_list), so the exported API is truthful. The fork's oEdtk::Infinite lands in oEUser (oEUser::Infinite: the COBOL and Infinite record readers) because it builds addresses through oEUser::Lib; the generic lib/oEdtk/Infinite.pm is a thin delegate keeping the fork's name. Extension points without a registry are added as lib/oEdtk/Ext.pm (D18): require_optional loads an optional companion module by its fixed name (oEUser::Lib, oEUser::Schema) and reports absence, and load_named_callable / call_named_callable resolve a Module::function name read from configuration (EDTK_ACQUIT_API) after validating it against a regular expression -- an absent key is a documented no-op, an invalid or unresolvable name is an explicit error. No oEdtk module refers to the corporate brand any more: the last four brand residues in the generic tree (two cgi-bin forms, the sample CSV, and t/20_fields.t) are replaced by CORP, so T08 is empty. The T02 API-gap ratchet loses the three whole-module lines (oEdtk::Utils, oEdtk::LaTeX, oEdtk::Infinite), and the oEUser load-gap ratchet empties (oEUser::Lib now compiles against the generic oEdtk).
    - tests: new t/int/19_user_extensions.t (T19: the fixed-name optional module, the named callable with its invalid/absent/uninstalled cases, and the generic delegates loading without oEUser), t/int/31_utils.t (T31: the generic text helpers, IDX_FORMAT, and the corporate delegates), t/int/33_latex.t (T33: every exported symbol defined, the latin-9 escaping table, the small builders and make_index) and the fixture t/lib/AcquitFixture.pm; oEUser/t/20_moved_modules.t (T62) gains the oEUser::Utils / oEUser::Infinite facet with their oEdtk delegates. The suite is 616 tests over 44 files (root) and 22 tests over 4 files (oEUser).
2.1109      2026-10-11
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: distribution tables (create_table_DISTRIB) now also create ix_<table>_job (ed_idjob) and ix_<table>_dtlot (ed_dtlot). The composite index leads with ed_idldoc, so the by-job predicate (agrege_idJob, _acheck_db_rotate) and the by-batch-date predicate (rotation) could not use it and fell back to a sequential scan; with the new indexes PostgreSQL chooses a bitmap index scan (EXPLAIN cost 1135 -> 684). Created through _db_do_ddl so "create index if not exists" stays portable across the five engines.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: the MySQL bulk load (_load_csv_mysql_local_infile) now runs ANALYZE TABLE after LOAD DATA LOCAL INFILE, in parity with the PostgreSQL COPY path, so the planner keeps fresh statistics after a large import.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: admin_optimize_db opens a single connection for the whole operation instead of reconnecting twice per table (24 connections for 12 tables), detects the driver once on the live handle, and declares its per-engine repair/optimize templates in one place (_db_maintenance_commands). PostgreSQL now uses VACUUM ANALYZE instead of VACUUM FULL (which took an exclusive lock and rewrote the table in the routine path); SQLite runs ANALYZE (it has no per-table VACUUM); MySQL keeps REPAIR/OPTIMIZE TABLE and Oracle is a no-op.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: db_backup_agent is no longer flagged deprecated (it is not a copy_table alias: it snapshots three tables and purges the rows older than EDTK_ENTIRE_YEARS_KEPT). Its three copy-pasted blocks are collapsed into a declarative loop; an already-existing archive (same-day re-run) is now kept as is instead of making CREATE TABLE ... AS SELECT fail; the routine accepts an optional CFG, so it is testable.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: SQLite can now be used as the main database and generate lot identifiers. create_lot_sequence creates the edtk_idlot_seq counter table on SQLite (0..999, wrapping) and Outmngr::_get_seqlot reads it back, building the "ISO week + day-of-week + 3-digit sequence" prefix in Perl (SQLite has neither SEQUENCE nor to_char). The Oracle and PostgreSQL paths are unchanged. The backup database remains a write-only buffer and does not generate identifiers.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: new public db_invalidate_meta_cache drops the column-metadata cache used by csv_import; schema_Create and schema_Upgrade call it so a later import re-reads the columns after a schema change. db_check_privileges now also probes INDEX, ALTER and SEQUENCE (in addition to CREATE and DROP), with no extra query per backend, and still never dies.
    - oEdtk::Outmngr: every warn statement now goes through &logger instead of writing straight to STDERR, so the messages carry the usual timestamp|level|PID prefix and obey $LOGGERLEVEL. Progression messages are logged at 6-INFO, truncation and "not enough pages" notices at 4-WARN, and the $@ database errors at 3-ALERT; the seven commented-out #warn "DEBUG: ..." lines became commented #&logger(7, ...). The missing "use oEdtk::logger qw(logger)" import was added (a &logger call already existed without it).
    - tests: new t/35_dbadmin_optimize.t (per-engine maintenance templates and an end-to-end run on SQLite), t/36_outmngr_seqlot.t (SQLite lot-id generation), t/37_dbadmin_backup_agent.t (archive-and-purge, same-day re-run), t/38_dbadmin_meta_cache.t (cache invalidation); t/33_dbadmin_privileges.t extended to the five rights; t/30_dbadmin_pure.t gained MariaDB and INSERT _sql_fixup cases. The suite is 415 tests over 18 files.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: $VERSION 2.1108 -> 2.1109.
    - oEdtk.pm: $VERSION 2.1108 -> 2.1109.

2.1108      2026-10-10
    - Every Perl module under lib/ and every script under tracker/ now follows rule that comments, POD and user-facing messages are written in English. Only text was changed: no identifier, hash key, column or table name, format string or use constant value was touched, and behaviour is unchanged. The accented (ISO-8859) source bytes were carried over through a byte-safe translator, and the whole test suite still passes.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: new public subroutine db_check_privileges($dbh, %opt) reports, without ever dying, whether the connected DB user may CREATE and DROP objects. It only reads the data dictionary (no DDL): PostgreSQL uses has_database_privilege / has_schema_privilege for CREATE and table ownership (pg_class.relowner) for DROP, MySQL/MariaDB parses SHOW GRANTS FOR CURRENT_USER() against the current schema (SELECT DATABASE()), Oracle reads USER_SYS_PRIVS / ROLE_SYS_PRIVS, SQLite (no privilege model) is assumed allowed, and an unknown or absent handle is left unchecked. Each missing right raises a non-blocking &logger(3, ...) alert.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: schema_Create and schema_Upgrade call db_check_privileges best-effort (under eval) right after the connection is established, so a missing CREATE / DROP right is reported up front rather than failing later on the DDL; the probe can never block the load.
    - tests: new t/33_dbadmin_privileges.t covers db_check_privileges with an in-memory SQLite handle plus a mock $dbh for the PostgreSQL, MySQL/MariaDB and Oracle branches; the t/31_dbadmin_sqlite.t assertion on the translated _get_col_meta message was updated.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: $VERSION 2.1107 → 2.1108.
    - oEdtk.pm: $VERSION 2.1106 → 2.1108.

2.1107      2026-10-10
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: dead code removed — the deprecated wrappers csv_import_deprecated_1, csv_import_deprecated_2, csv_import_deprecated_3, insert_tData_deprecated_1, insert_tData_deprecated_2, _get_col_meta_deprecated_1, _get_col_meta_deprecated_2, _db_check_driver_name_deprecated and admin_optimize_db_deprecated (731 lines).
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: $VERSION 2.1106 → 2.1107.

2.1106      2026-10-10
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: fix a quadratic hot spot in the PostgreSQL COPY path. _pg_csv_supplier used to accumulate each 1 MiB block by string concatenation and then reset the buffer, a pattern that is quadratic in the block size and dominated the whole load — it even made this "optimized" loader slower than the previous temporary-file one. Blocks are now built by collecting the cleaned rows in an array and joining them once per block. Measured on a 2 002 280-row fixture the load drops from 722.7 s to 195.8 s (3.7x faster); the 50 057-row fixture goes from 19.0 s to 5.7 s.
    - tests: new fixture generator tracker/dev/build/tests/data/tracker-test-Metadata-heavy2M.pl, which rebuilds a two-million-row CSV from tracker-test-Metadata-heavy.csv by repeating it and rewriting ED_SEQDOC so the edtk_metadata primary key stays unique (all other columns are copied byte for byte). The generated CSV (~670 MB) is listed in .gitignore and rebuilt on demand.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: $VERSION 2.1105 → 2.1106.
    - oEdtk.pm: $VERSION 2.1105 → 2.1106.

2.1105      2026-10-09
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: PostgreSQL COPY ... FROM STDIN bulk load no longer writes a temporary cleaned copy of the CSV: rows are cleaned and serialized on the fly and streamed straight into COPY through the new private helper _pg_csv_supplier. Per-row cleaning is fused with serialization in the new private helper _pg_csv_row, which takes positional column metadata, so no closure or hash lookup runs per value; the re-encode to the session client_encoding is applied once per block (Encode is concatenative). COPY data is now fed in whole blocks (new constant PG_COPY_BLOCK_SIZE, 1 MiB) instead of one line per pg_putcopydata call, and the File::Temp dependency is dropped.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: _pg_deferrable_ddl accepts a new $defer_pk flag; passing pg_copy_defer_pk => 1 to csv_import also drops and rebuilds the target table's primary key around the COPY. A primary key referenced by an external foreign key is still left untouched, and if any deferred DDL cannot be dropped the load falls back to the non-deferred path.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: $VERSION 2.1104 → 2.1105.
    - oEdtk.pm: $VERSION 2.1104 → 2.1105.

2.1104      2026-10-08
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: the bulk CSV loaders now log an informational line stating that the insertion is done in bulk, which method is used, and how many rows were injected. All three paths report it — MySQL LOAD DATA INFILE, MySQL LOAD DATA LOCAL INFILE and PostgreSQL COPY ... FROM STDIN. The row count is derived from the CSV normalization pass; the two MySQL INFILE paths count records through the new private helper _count_csv_rows (Text::CSV getline, used so a quoted field may span several physical lines). Return values are unchanged.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: PostgreSQL COPY ... FROM STDIN performance — the load now runs inside a single transaction and, before the COPY, drops the target table's secondary indexes and unique / foreign-key constraints so they are rebuilt in one bulk pass afterwards instead of being maintained row by row during the load. The objects to defer are collected from pg_catalog by the new private helper _pg_deferrable_ddl; primary keys, and any index on which a foreign key depends, are left untouched.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: the COPY transaction relaxes synchronous_commit (SET LOCAL synchronous_commit = off) so the commit does not wait for the WAL flush — transaction-scoped and reversible, with no change to the schema — and runs ANALYZE on the target table afterwards to refresh the planner statistics. New constants PG_COPY_SYNC_OFF and PG_COPY_ANALYZE.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: the optimized load is atomic — a failure rolls back both the data and the deferred DDL, and if a DDL object cannot be dropped the load is retried once without deferral (a caller-managed transaction with AutoCommit already off is left open). Passing pg_copy_optimize => 0 to csv_import keeps the historical plain COPY. The COPY itself was extracted into the new private helper _pg_copy_stdin; new private helper _pg_quote_ident.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: $VERSION 2.1101 → 2.1104.
    - oEdtk.pm: $VERSION 2.1102 → 2.1104.

2.1102      2026-10-06
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: new csv_import fast path for PostgreSQL using COPY ... FROM STDIN, the native equivalent of the MySQL LOAD DATA LOCAL INFILE path. It is selected automatically for the Pg driver when the import mode is not "merge"; rows are first cleaned through the same _get_col_meta / _make_clean_val pipeline into a temporary file, so truncation and '' => NULL conversion match the row-by-row path. New private helpers _load_csv_pg_copy, _pg_csv_field and _pg_encoding_name.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: _load_csv_pg_copy reads records with Text::CSV getline (instead of parse) so that a quoted field may span several physical lines; COPY runs with FORMAT csv, the current separator/quote characters and NULL '' so an unquoted empty field is read back as NULL.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: _load_csv_pg_copy re-encodes each row to the session client_encoding (from SHOW client_encoding, mapped to an Encode name) before pg_putcopydata, so multibyte values are stored correctly. New dependencies: File::Temp and Encode.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: $VERSION 2.1071 → 2.1101 during the PostgreSQL COPY work.
    - New test suite under t/ (Test::More): 00_load.t, 10_main_date.t, 11_main_num.t, 12_main_text.t, 20_fields.t, 21_dict_tags.t, 30_dbadmin_pure.t, 31_dbadmin_sqlite.t, 40_tracking_validate.t and 50_edms_pure.t, plus t/lib/TestOEdtk.pm (shared helpers), t/edtk.ini (test configuration) and t/test_csv_pg_copy.pl (PostgreSQL COPY import check).
    - README.md: the former plain-text README was merged into README.md and the CONTENT OF THIS ARCHIVE section rewritten with the actual package tree; copyright year updated 2024 → 2026.
    - oEdtk.pm: $VERSION 2.1071 → 2.1102.

2.1071      2026-07-01
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: _get_col_meta now distinguishes text types (varchar, character varying, char, bpchar, text) from numeric and date/time types. The truncation size is only used for text columns; numeric and date/time columns get a new blank_to_null flag. This fixes erroneous truncation of values on PostgreSQL (e.g. a date 2026-07-09 was being truncated to 2026 because column_info returns the internal storage size for non-text types).
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: _make_clean_val — empty-string → undef conversion now applies to both numeric AND date/time columns (blank_to_null), fixing PostgreSQL "invalid input syntax for type date" errors.
