2.1064      2026-06-04
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: $VERSION = 2.1063; new $VERSION_TXT (version with dots replaced by underscores, used in index names). admin_check_db renamed to acheck_db_admin_on_connect; private _drop_table renamed to public db_drop_table (new export).
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: massive SQL rewrite to lowercase keywords and identifiers throughout (all maintenance queries, purges, rotations, table creation) for portability across MySQL / PostgreSQL / Oracle / SQLite. _sql_fixup gained a third $mysqlCasse argument: for MySQL the whole SQL is uppercased (except INSERT/REPLACE statements); for PostgreSQL empty strings '' are converted to NULL in VALUES/SET clauses; VARCHAR2→VARCHAR conversion is now case-insensitive.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: insert_tData rewritten — driver-aware identifier case normalization (_norm_identifiers, uc for MySQL/MariaDB, lc otherwise), column metadata lookup (_get_col_meta via DBI column_info, with a SELECT * WHERE 1=0 fallback for drivers like SQLite), and value cleaning (_make_clean_val: empty string → undef for numeric columns, truncation to declared column size). Old implementations kept as insert_tData_deprecated_1 / insert_tData_deprecated_2.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: csv_import rewritten with the same metadata/cleaning pipeline; old versions kept as csv_import_deprecated_1/2/3; new private helpers _norm_identifiers, _get_col_meta, _make_clean_val.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: db_connect — FetchHashKeyName is now configurable via EDTK_DB_FetchHashKeyName (default NAME_uc); the TRACKING table is auto-created on connect if missing (_table_exists); the auto DB check now only runs when EDTK_DB_CHECK_AUTO is explicitly YES (previously defaulted to YES when unset); calls acheck_db_admin_on_connect instead of admin_check_db.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: new _table_exists helper (DBI table_info); new acheck_db_admin2 (on-demand maintenance job) built on new _db_maintenance and _db_with_lock (locking via an edtk_admin insert).
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: _db_check_driver_name hardened (returns "NC" for an invalid/unconnected $dbh); old version kept as _db_check_driver_name_deprecated.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: admin_optimize_db rewritten — driver detected per connection, no-op select 1 for NC/Oracle, REPAIR TABLE/OPTIMIZE TABLE for MySQL, VACUUM FULL for PostgreSQL; old version kept as admin_optimize_db_deprecated.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: index names changed from ix.$VERSION.$table (dot-separated) to ix_${table}_${VERSION_TXT} (underscore-separated, portable) and use create index if not exists. create_lot_sequence now issues create sequence if not exists edtk_idlot minvalue 0 maxvalue 999 cycle through _sql_fixup.
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: all column-definition arrays (@TRACKER_COLS, @DISTRIB_COLS, @AGREGE_COLS, @INDEX_COLS) converted to lowercase column names. create_table_OUTMNGR: ed_ididx no longer NOT NULL; ed_nbdocpli and ed_numpgpli no longer NOT NULL. move_table, db_backup_agent, schema_Upgrade, schema_Create: lowercase SQL and _sql_fixup(..., 'casse').
    - lib/oEdtk/logger2.pm: package renamed from oEdtk::logger2 to oEdtk::logger (the file is still logger2.pm); $VERSION = 1.9062. New exported subs set_logger_level($) and set_warn_to_logger(). Letter-based level normalization: new %hLETTER_LEVEL maps letters (H, F, C, E, S, X, W, A, I, P, L, D, U) to numeric levels; logger() now accepts a letter as the level or as the modifier argument. _DEBUG_ and _CONTXT_ constants swapped: _DEBUG_ = 7, _CONTXT_ = 8 (previously reversed). Log line format changed to >%date| %-7s|FH-%07d|PID-%s|last RC: %0.3d| %s|last RC: %0.3d-%s. logger() return value changed: scalar context returns $rcLogger[0] (or the joined string for FAIL level); list context returns @rcLogger. usage_logger renamed to logger_help; logger_help now takes an optional argument controlling whether logger_rc_list is printed.
    - oEdtk::Tracking: track sub — the table name is now uppercased when the driver is MySQL (identifier case fix); stats_week, stats_iddest, stats_month: SQL converted to lowercase.
    - oEdtk::Config: use oEdtk::logger now explicitly imports qw(logger $LOGGERLEVEL $WARN2LOGGER).
