0.7014      2012-01-04
    - oEdtk.pm: oEdtk_version() renamed to oEdtk_release(); the END block now prints oEdtk_release() (banner text changed to include daunay@cpan.org).
    - oEdtk::Main: new exported subs oe_CAP_sans_accents, oe_char_xlate, oe_list_encodings; oe_oe_uc_sans_accents removed (renamed to oe_CAP_sans_accents). New sub oe_char_xlate($;$) translates characters in a string using the EDTK_DICO_XLAT dictionary (section parameter, default DEFAULT), memoized in a static $_DICO_CHAR. New sub oe_list_encodings lists encodings available on the machine via Encode->encodings(). oe_clean_addr_line: hardcoded punctuation/special-char replacements are commented out and replaced by a call to oe_char_xlate($$rLine, 'ADDRESS') — character cleaning is now dictionary-driven. oe_new_job: new --input_code option; input file opened with encoding layer <:encoding(...); output file opened with >:encoding(...) using new config key EDTK_OUT_ENCODING (default utf8); outfile now derived from $params->{'outfile'}. oe_app_usage: usage text updated (documents --input_code); now calls oe_list_encodings(). One system() error check changed from $? to $@. END block no longer prints the version banner.
    - oEdtk::Dict: substitue_char renamed to substitue; now iterates the dictionary and converts keys matching chr(N) into the actual character before substitution — dictionary keys can now be written as chr(123) to target special characters.
    - oEdtk::Doc: new method char_xlate($$) translates characters using the EDTK_DICO_XLAT dictionary (section passed as argument), memoized in a static $_DICO_CHAR.
    - oEdtk::TexTag: now warns (INFO) when a tag name contains digits (previously a commented-out die); escape() now calls oEdtk::Doc::char_xlate($new, "LATEX") for special-character translation; adds replacement of \"{} by \textquotestraightdblbase{}.
    - oEdtk::TexDoc: only version bump and added trailing 1;.
    - oEdtk::Record: new fields_offset attribute (default 10) and set_fields_offset method; parse() now uses the configurable offset instead of a hardcoded 8-character prefix.
    - oEdtk::RecordParser: new() dies if the filehandle is undefined; parser is now fully configurable: new attributes skip_line ('FLUX'), mute_record ('ENTETE'), mute_id ('ENT'), line_record ('LIGNE'), key_offset (153), key_size (10), denormalized ('OPTION'), denormalized_split_motif, with setter methods; next() uses these configurable values; line-record parsing now captures the key and data separately (key whitespace-stripped); current line stored in $self->{'line'}.
    - oEdtk::Tracking: new BEGIN block installs $SIG{'__WARN__'} and $SIG{'__DIE__'} handlers that call track('Warn'/'Halt', 1, $msg) when signal tracking is active; new() enables signal tracking if config EDTK_TRACK_SIG is set (and not 'no'); track() — new ED_MESSAGE column handling (data values concatenated into the message); ED_SOURCE now also set for Halt events; user key columns (ED_K{i}_NAME/VAL) are only filled when more than one data value is passed (a single value goes to the message column).
    - oEdtk::DBAdmin: tracking table schema — new ED_MESSAGE VARCHAR2(256) column added; lots table schema — ED_REFENC column moved (no functional change); error messages prefixed with ERROR:; one WARN level changed to INFO.
    - oEdtk::Outmngr: omgr_check_acquit SQL — ORDER BY now includes STATUS; report format string adjusted. omgr_stats SQL — table name now from $cfg->{'EDTK_STATS_OUTMNGR'} instead of hardcoded EDTK_INDEX. Several WARN messages downgraded to INFO; END banner commented out.
    - oEdtk::EDMS: zip-creation sub now returns 1; error messages prefixed with ERROR:.
    - oEdtk::Run: several subs now return 1 explicitly; one WARN downgraded to INFO.
    - oEdtk::C7Tag / oEdtk::SignedField / oEdtk::trackEdtk: only WARN → INFO message-level changes.
    - lib scripts: cob2pm.pl — usage() now exits; identifier regex allows names longer than 31 chars; strips first-column comments; replaces _ with -; strips trailing whitespace; more detailed error messages. index_Run_lot.pl — mail subject no longer prefixed with EDTK_TYPE_ENV. check_oEdtk_ini.pl, db_historicize_*.pl, db_move.pl — print → warn, WARN → INFO. index_Block_refs.pl — WARN → INFO; abort message changed to die "ERROR: abort request". index_Statistics.pl, params_Export.pl, params_Import.pl — error messages prefixed with ERROR:. libDev.pm — message prefixes standardized (INFO :/ERROR:); one error check changed from $? to $@.
    - MANIFEST, MANIFEST.SKIP, README: trailing-space changes only. META.yml: version bump only.

